1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,149
The sky tears open over the final battlefield.

2
00:00:03,149 --> 00:00:06,860
Red light, black light, and a whole world holding its breath.

3
00:00:07,155 --> 00:00:10,170
[LIEBE] Asta! Wake up! Asta!

4
00:00:10,372 --> 00:00:15,774
Asta falls, and the world goes silent. Then church bells. Cold sheets.

5
00:00:15,774 --> 00:00:21,022
Small, trembling hands. Same bed, same church, same cracked ceiling.

6
00:00:21,299 --> 00:00:23,314
Asta was never supposed to have magic.

7
00:00:23,314 --> 00:00:26,709
He was supposed to wait fifteen years in the dirt for a miracle.

8
00:00:26,998 --> 00:00:30,435
What if he remembered everything? The Spade raid.

9
00:00:30,435 --> 00:00:34,013
The betrayals. Every name, every face, every grave.

10
00:00:34,299 --> 00:00:37,390
And the brother sealed inside the wall of Hage's tower.

11
00:00:37,390 --> 00:00:39,919
All of it, in the head of a six year old boy.

12
00:00:43,789 --> 00:00:48,944
The wind in Hage comes down off the demon skull, and nobody ever thinks twice about it.

13
00:00:48,944 --> 00:00:54,809
Asta thinks about nothing else. He stands at the church fence, eyes closed, and feels the air lean.

14
00:00:55,081 --> 00:00:58,073
Ki. The breath and the heartbeat of the world.

15
00:00:58,073 --> 00:01:01,196
A body with no magic can still learn to hear it.

16
00:01:01,456 --> 00:01:02,567
The air shifts.

17
00:01:02,567 --> 00:01:08,416
Three seconds later, Yuno's gust slams the laundry line, and every sheet snaps.

18
00:01:08,679 --> 00:01:13,084
[YUNO] Hey. You looked at the sheets before my wind even moved. How?

19
00:01:13,290 --> 00:01:14,955
[ASTA] Heh. Lucky guess.

20
00:01:15,141 --> 00:01:19,478
Yuno is six, and still a crybaby. Last time, Asta mocked him for it.

21
00:01:19,478 --> 00:01:21,966
This time, he hands him a handkerchief.

22
00:01:22,283 --> 00:01:26,579
[YUNO] I wasn't crying! It was the wind, okay?

23
00:01:26,798 --> 00:01:29,143
[ASTA] Sure it was. Totally the wind.

24
00:01:29,309 --> 00:01:33,505
[YUNO] Why are you being nice to me? It's weird. What do you want?

25
00:01:33,668 --> 00:01:35,123
[ASTA] Call it an investment.

26
00:01:35,416 --> 00:01:40,691
It confuses everyone. The loudest kid in Hage has gone quiet, and he watches everything.

27
00:01:40,691 --> 00:01:45,006
Then Sister Lily crosses the yard, and an old habit wakes up on its own.

28
00:01:45,312 --> 00:01:47,537
[ASTA] Sister Lily, marry me!

29
00:01:47,713 --> 00:01:49,658
[SISTER LILY] Oh, Asta. You know the rule.

30
00:01:49,842 --> 00:01:52,409
He feels her weight shift a heartbeat early.

31
00:01:52,409 --> 00:01:55,442
And for the first time in history, Asta steps aside.

32
00:01:55,757 --> 00:01:59,362
[FATHER ORSI] It missed! Lily's fist missed! That's never happened!

33
00:01:59,542 --> 00:02:02,735
[SISTER LILY] Oh my. Asta, you're growing up so fast.

34
00:02:03,003 --> 00:02:08,495
At seven, Asta asks Yuno for a blindfold, then tells him to throw everything he has.

35
00:02:08,495 --> 00:02:14,183
Wind blades. Pebbles. A gust meant to knock him flat. He slips between them like smoke.

36
00:02:14,522 --> 00:02:15,971
[YUNO] How did you know?

37
00:02:16,181 --> 00:02:19,816
[ASTA] Throw harder. You breathe in right before you cast.

38
00:02:20,155 --> 00:02:24,151
Yuno goes very still. He isn't used to being the one who's behind.

39
00:02:24,151 --> 00:02:25,725
And he hates how it feels.

40
00:02:26,053 --> 00:02:29,726
[YUNO] Then I'll learn not to. I'll be Wizard King first, you'll see.

41
00:02:29,899 --> 00:02:32,704
[ASTA] Try it. I'm still beating you there, Yuno.

42
00:02:32,972 --> 00:02:36,837
Season after season, he trains the only thing nobody can take from him.

43
00:02:36,837 --> 00:02:40,702
And every night, he climbs to the roof and looks at the grimoire tower.

44
00:02:41,026 --> 00:02:43,343
Because he knows what is sleeping in its wall.

45
00:02:43,343 --> 00:02:45,861
And he knows exactly how long it has been waiting.

46
00:02:49,738 --> 00:02:55,921
Age ten. Midnight. The grimoire tower is empty, and Asta knows which stone to press.

47
00:02:55,921 --> 00:03:00,338
He follows the draft, cold and thin, to a crack in the wall.

48
00:03:00,606 --> 00:03:04,090
Behind the cracked stone lies a filthy, tattered book.

49
00:03:04,090 --> 00:03:07,186
Five leaves. He's waited four years to touch it.

50
00:03:07,487 --> 00:03:12,129
His fingers close on the cover, and the tower vanishes. Black water.

51
00:03:12,129 --> 00:03:17,112
No floor, no sky. Something vast turns over in the dark, and it's hungry.

52
00:03:17,404 --> 00:03:19,688
Chains of old black light hang from nowhere,

53
00:03:19,688 --> 00:03:22,024
and every single one of them is aimed at him.

54
00:03:22,328 --> 00:03:27,998
[LIEBE] A magicless brat, walking right into my mouth. How convenient.

55
00:03:28,197 --> 00:03:34,217
[LIEBE] Devils hate humans. I hate you most. I'll be wearing you by morning.

56
00:03:34,536 --> 00:03:35,870
Asta doesn't raise a hand.

57
00:03:35,870 --> 00:03:39,461
He just looks up, the way you look at someone you've missed for years.

58
00:03:39,790 --> 00:03:42,560
[LIEBE] Why aren't you scared, boy?

59
00:03:42,758 --> 00:03:43,868
[ASTA] Your name is Liebe.

60
00:03:44,175 --> 00:03:48,130
[LIEBE] Who told you that? Nobody knows that name.

61
00:03:48,296 --> 00:03:51,956
[ASTA] Your mother named you. Her name was Licita.

62
00:03:52,158 --> 00:03:54,873
[LIEBE] Don't. Don't say that name.

63
00:03:55,091 --> 00:03:58,301
[ASTA] Licita. She held you until the very end.

64
00:03:58,496 --> 00:03:59,856
[LIEBE] I said don't!

65
00:04:00,067 --> 00:04:05,547
The dark shudders. Claws that were closing stop, trembling, an inch from his face.

66
00:04:05,881 --> 00:04:11,751
[LIEBE] She died. She sealed me in this filth and died. What do you know?

67
00:04:11,944 --> 00:04:15,089
[ASTA] That she chose you. Every single time.

68
00:04:15,809 --> 00:04:16,322
Nothing.

69
00:04:16,322 --> 00:04:21,199
For a long time, only the sound of something enormous trying not to breathe.

70
00:04:21,461 --> 00:04:22,856
[ASTA] She was my mother too.

71
00:04:23,116 --> 00:04:25,561
[LIEBE] No. That's not possible.

72
00:04:25,751 --> 00:04:28,691
[ASTA] She left me at a church door so I'd live.

73
00:04:29,012 --> 00:04:30,409
[LIEBE] Who are you?

74
00:04:30,745 --> 00:04:33,015
[ASTA] Your brother. And I'm late.

75
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:36,760
[ASTA] Last time, I was fifteen years late.

76
00:04:37,070 --> 00:04:40,090
[LIEBE] Last time? What does that mean?

77
00:04:40,266 --> 00:04:42,956
[ASTA] Later. First, let me sit down.

78
00:04:43,147 --> 00:04:44,927
[LIEBE] What do you want from me?

79
00:04:45,095 --> 00:04:47,825
[ASTA] Just to sit here a minute. With my brother.

80
00:04:48,114 --> 00:04:51,229
[LIEBE] Tch. You're the dumbest human I've ever met.

81
00:04:51,394 --> 00:04:53,494
[ASTA] Probably. I've been told.

82
00:04:53,754 --> 00:05:01,772
Outside, the dawn bell rolls over Hage. Asta climbs out of the tower with dust on his hands and no fear at all.

83
00:05:01,772 --> 00:05:06,539
Behind him, in the wall, a devil lies still. Not trapped. Waiting.

84
00:05:10,043 --> 00:05:13,738
Five years. By day, Ki footwork until his legs shake.

85
00:05:13,738 --> 00:05:20,083
By night, he sits against the tower wall and talks. About bread. About Yuno. About the sky.

86
00:05:20,421 --> 00:05:23,736
[ASTA] Today Yuno tried to cut a tree. The tree won.

87
00:05:23,915 --> 00:05:28,970
[LIEBE] You're boring me to death, human. Bread? Seriously, bread?

88
00:05:29,169 --> 00:05:30,609
[ASTA] Then why do you keep answering?

89
00:05:30,809 --> 00:05:34,334
[LIEBE] I'm stuck in a book. Echoes are all I get.

90
00:05:34,604 --> 00:05:37,116
The book won't open before the ceremony.

91
00:05:37,116 --> 00:05:40,884
So Asta waits, again. But this time, he isn't waiting alone.

92
00:05:41,209 --> 00:05:46,029
[LIEBE] Make the contract. Master and servant. That's how it works.

93
00:05:46,244 --> 00:05:48,794
[ASTA] No. Equals, or nothing.

94
00:05:49,003 --> 00:05:53,904
[LIEBE] Tch. Fine. Equals. Whatever. Like I care.

95
00:05:54,196 --> 00:05:57,893
Fifteen. The tower hall is packed with trembling children.

96
00:05:57,893 --> 00:06:01,526
Yuno steps forward, and a four-leaf grimoire answers him.

97
00:06:01,835 --> 00:06:05,588
Then it's Asta's turn. Nothing. No light, no book.

98
00:06:05,588 --> 00:06:08,515
Only laughter, rolling across the hall.

99
00:06:08,850 --> 00:06:11,695
[LIEBE] They're laughing at you. Doesn't that bother you?

100
00:06:11,913 --> 00:06:14,638
[ASTA] Not anymore. I know how this ends.

101
00:06:14,978 --> 00:06:19,674
Exactly as before, down to the last giggle. And this time, Asta smiles.

102
00:06:19,674 --> 00:06:26,553
On the road home, Revchi steps out of the trees, chains hissing at his wrists. He wants Yuno's grimoire.

103
00:06:26,832 --> 00:06:30,823
He doesn't notice the magicless boy who's already standing behind him.

104
00:06:30,823 --> 00:06:31,792
Nobody ever does.

105
00:06:32,077 --> 00:06:37,042
[ASTA] Revchi. Chain Magic. Thrown out of the Purple Orcas in disgrace.

106
00:06:37,207 --> 00:06:40,254
[REVCHI] Magicless trash like you has no right to—

107
00:06:40,473 --> 00:06:41,298
[ASTA] Skip it.

108
00:06:41,571 --> 00:06:46,402
Behind them the tower groans. A crack tears up the wall, and the stone gives way.

109
00:06:46,402 --> 00:06:51,651
The five-leaf grimoire rips itself free and tears across the sky, straight for his hand.

110
00:06:51,980 --> 00:06:56,094
[LIEBE] Hurry up, partner. I'm getting bored over here.

111
00:06:56,292 --> 00:06:59,961
The Demon-Slayer Sword drops into his hand. One swing.

112
00:06:59,961 --> 00:07:03,697
Revchi's chains don't break. They simply stop existing.

113
00:07:04,022 --> 00:07:07,367
[LIEBE] Ha! Now that's what I'm talking about.

114
00:07:07,527 --> 00:07:10,852
[REVCHI] My chains! What did you do to my chains?

115
00:07:11,045 --> 00:07:13,250
[YUNO] You've been hiding something since we were six.

116
00:07:13,416 --> 00:07:14,771
[ASTA] Only a few things.

117
00:07:14,936 --> 00:07:18,396
[YUNO] Fine. Keep your secrets. Just leave me an enemy next time.

118
00:07:18,597 --> 00:07:20,362
[ASTA] Then be faster, Yuno.

119
00:07:20,558 --> 00:07:22,243
[YUNO] Hmph. I was letting you have it.

120
00:07:25,725 --> 00:07:29,365
The Royal Capital. Banners, towers, ten thousand voices.

121
00:07:29,365 --> 00:07:32,745
Every hopeful in the kingdom, packed into one arena.

122
00:07:33,036 --> 00:07:38,762
And across the field, a man in black, cigarette burning low. Yami Sukehiro. Alive.

123
00:07:38,762 --> 00:07:45,466
Asta's breath catches. He remembers losing that man, and now he's standing right there, yawning.

124
00:07:45,792 --> 00:07:48,822
[YAMI] Kid. Why are you looking at me like I died?

125
00:07:48,986 --> 00:07:50,901
[ASTA] No reason. Really.

126
00:07:51,091 --> 00:07:53,526
[YAMI] Stop it. You're creeping me out, kid.

127
00:07:53,725 --> 00:07:55,540
[ASTA] Sorry. Long story.

128
00:07:55,867 --> 00:07:57,739
His match lasts one breath.

129
00:07:57,739 --> 00:08:02,247
Asta reads the swing, steps inside it, and ends it with one move.

130
00:08:02,516 --> 00:08:05,161
[YAMI] Not bad, brat. Where'd you learn that?

131
00:08:05,353 --> 00:08:06,988
[ASTA] A very patient teacher.

132
00:08:07,191 --> 00:08:10,021
[YAMI] Tch. Whoever he is, he owes me a drink.

133
00:08:10,339 --> 00:08:13,366
The arena goes silent. Then one hand goes up.

134
00:08:13,366 --> 00:08:16,999
Then another. Hands that never went up for him before.

135
00:08:17,623 --> 00:08:24,632
Noelle Silva. Last time, her water magic ran wild for months, and Asta watched her become the pride of her house.

136
00:08:24,632 --> 00:08:29,098
Today she's at the edge of the field, spilling water over her own boots.

137
00:08:29,426 --> 00:08:32,821
[NOELLE] Eyes off, commoner. My magic is just having a bad day.

138
00:08:33,019 --> 00:08:36,291
[ASTA] It's not a bad day. You're aiming at your family's approval.

139
00:08:36,291 --> 00:08:38,309
[ASTA] Aim at something you want to protect.

140
00:08:38,483 --> 00:08:41,758
[NOELLE] Don't get the wrong idea. I didn't ask a commoner for advice.

141
00:08:41,944 --> 00:08:48,737
But her fingers close anyway. She thinks of nothing she has to win, only of what she'd stand in front of.

142
00:08:48,737 --> 00:08:53,524
And the water rises in her bare palm. No wand. Round, and perfectly still.

143
00:08:53,842 --> 00:08:56,987
[NOELLE] It's holding. It's actually holding. It's listening to me.

144
00:08:57,598 --> 00:08:59,773
[ASTA] Yeah. That one's all yours.

145
00:09:00,054 --> 00:09:03,224
[YAMI] Listen, brat. The Black Bulls aren't exactly—

146
00:09:03,384 --> 00:09:06,334
[ASTA] Black Bulls. I'm in. Sign me up.

147
00:09:06,649 --> 00:09:09,692
Across the arena, Yuno signs with the Golden Dawn.

148
00:09:09,692 --> 00:09:14,744
His wind moves before he breathes in. That's what years of chasing one boy will do.

149
00:09:15,047 --> 00:09:16,507
[YUNO] Don't fall behind, Asta.

150
00:09:16,709 --> 00:09:17,974
[ASTA] Don't trip, Yuno.

151
00:09:18,261 --> 00:09:20,950
On the arena floor, Asta closes his eyes.

152
00:09:20,950 --> 00:09:23,966
The captains' box becomes a map of heartbeats.

153
00:09:24,301 --> 00:09:26,320
He knows exactly where to look.

154
00:09:26,320 --> 00:09:32,051
William Vangeance sits very still, and inside him there are two Ki. Two lives. One body.

155
00:09:32,315 --> 00:09:34,707
But this time, someone feels it back.

156
00:09:34,707 --> 00:09:40,525
Behind William's calm eyes, Patolli turns, slow as a blade, toward the boy who is looking.

157
00:09:41,126 --> 00:09:46,476
Above them all, Wizard King Julius Novachrono tilts his head. He's watching the boy.

158
00:09:46,790 --> 00:09:49,425
[JULIUS] Oh? This boy's time doesn't move like ours.

159
00:09:49,425 --> 00:09:52,060
[JULIUS] Someone has wound it back. How interesting.

160
00:09:52,633 --> 00:09:59,380
That night, on the road to the Black Bulls' hideout, the air above the trees folds open like torn cloth.

161
00:09:59,380 --> 00:10:05,153
White-robed mages step out, one after another. The Eye of the Midnight Sun. Months early.

162
00:10:05,469 --> 00:10:09,074
None of this happened in his first life. Asta stops walking.

163
00:10:09,074 --> 00:10:12,199
The future he memorized has just stopped being true.

164
00:10:12,949 --> 00:10:13,623
In Part Two,

165
00:10:13,623 --> 00:10:18,564
the Eye of the Midnight Sun comes for the one boy who knows exactly how this story ends.

166
00:10:18,855 --> 00:10:23,225
[ASTA] Wind's changed. Fine. Then I'll learn to read it all over again.

